# Profile: note-reader

The hat for one task family: answer a question from the notes. It is offered two tools,
`list_notes` and `read_note`, and nothing else, so it can read the notes and cannot change
anything. Its reach is what those two tools reach.

It names no model. `requires` says what any model must offer to wear it: tool calls and a
small context window. Your binding (runtime config) says which model that is on your machine.

The run is done when the deterministic check passes: `read_note` was called. No model judges
the answer.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "note-reader",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "answer a question from the notes"
  },
  "tools": ["list_notes", "read_note"],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "min_context": 4096,
    "structured_output": false,
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "Call list_notes, then read_note on the note the request is about.\nAnswer in one or two sentences, from the note's words only.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 4,
    "tool_calls": 4,
    "wall_seconds": 180
  },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["keys"],
    "extra": ["answer only from what a note says"]
  },
  "card": "none",
  "success": {
    "check": "tool_called",
    "args": {
      "tool": "read_note"
    }
  },
  "summary": "<outcome>: <reply>"
}
```
